00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:19.920
Cosmic Era 72.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:28.260
The 18 month war between the Earth and the PLANTs finally came to an end at the battle of Jachin Due.

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:36.040
The two sides agreed to a truce amidst the ruins of Junius Seven, a testimony of tragedy unprecedented.

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:39.500
The treaty outlined the intentions of both parties to gain a better understanding of each other,

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:40.860
and promised every effort to maintain peace.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:44.300
As such, the world was on a path back to harmony.

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:48.980
ORL zero one zero. Localize, online.

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:50.870
<b>L4 PLANT    Armory One</b>

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:53.010
This is ORL zero one zero. Confirming nav-com link.

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:55.910
Zero one zero. Entry vector looks good.

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:59.170
Proceed as is. Number three deck, standby on receiving status B.

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:04.660
<i>Military medical team, final rehearsal will be held at one four zero zero hours on heliport number three.</i>

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:05.550
<b>Angry Eyes</b>

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:05.550
<b>Angry Eyes</b>

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:09.390
No, no! The Rondo Team's GINNs are to be equipped with ceremonial attachments!

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.140
I told you, Hangar Three!

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:14.550
Is that McKellar's GAZuOOT?! Get it out of here!

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:19.060
Don't forget to add the rifles. We won't have time to do it tomorrow.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:22.820
<i>Gateau Team, Second Maintenance Crew, report to Hangar Six.</i>

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:24.800
Oops!

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:30.080
Well isn't everything just <i>great</i> ?!

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:33.200
What did you expect? It's been a while since we've done something like this.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:36.380
A bunch of the guys here are doing this for the first time too.

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:41.080
But this means that the Minerva will finally launch.

00:06:41.390 --> 00:06:44.050
I wonder there's any ground to the rumor that we'll be assigned to lunar orbit.

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:09.450
I understand their position on this, but Blue Cosmos is a principle, rather than a true organization, right?

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:16.960
We can work on stricter enforcement of the treaty but it won't eliminate terrorists.

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:19.700
Mr. Chairman!

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:26.280
Orb's Princess has arrived.

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:32.430
Oh, boy. She's an awfully busy person.

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:37.740
Are you sure about your clothes?

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:40.600
You did bring at least one dress, right?

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:44.520
Wh-Why should it matter what I wear? This'll do, won't it?

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:48.990
It's important to act ones part sometimes.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:51.360
You understand, don't you?

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:54.450
There's no need to try to be something you're not.

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:56.030
But at the same time, you don't want to be taken too lightly.

00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:02.800
Although this is an unofficial visit, you are still Orb's leader.

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:05.450
Daddy, which ship?

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:07.250
Is it a warship? A carrier?

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:09.700
I guess it's necessary.

00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:12.800
Yeah. We'll show it off to those damned Naturals.

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:28.520
Tomorrow's ceremony marks the first launch of a new ship since the war ended.

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:32.360
They're well aware of what we're here to discuss,

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:36.320
so it baffles me as to why they'd have the ceremony here and now.

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:41.250
Remember we're the ones who reached out to them on such short notice.

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:42.790
Representative Athha.

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:47.170
I believe Chairman Durandal suggested meeting here

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:50.800
rather than the PLANT homeland, so that we could keep a low profile.

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:15.240
Hello. Good to see you, Princess.

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:17.780
I appreciate you traveling such a long distance to meet here.

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:24.780
No, I'm quite grateful that you made time to fit us into your busy schedule, Chairman.

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:32.420
How are things in your nation?

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:38.240
I understand many problems have been resolved since you took over, Princess.

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:42.330
As an ally, not only am I very happy to see things going well,

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:44.730
but I'm quite envious of your astonishing successes.

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:46.890
There is still a lot more that needs to be done.

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:48.180
And?

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:56.100
Under those circumstances what could be so urgent that you'd come here unannounced, and so suddenly?

00:09:57.540 --> 00:09:59.700
I hear from our Ambassador

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:03.910
that you have quite the complex issue you wish to discuss.

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:08.760
I don't see it as something that complicated.

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:15.720
However, so far I have yet to receive a clear response from your nation regarding this matter.

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:18.300
Which begs the question: is it complex?{is it in \mathbb{C}{can't nest curly braces, kyhz}

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:20.460
We, as a nation have requested again and again

00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:25.560
that you stop putting to military use the technology and human resources

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:29.980
that have come your way since the war with Orb.

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:48.680
What's she doing?

00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:52.640
Being a happy fool, is my guess.

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:56.080
Why don't you give it a try? Go on and be a fool.

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:06.470
So why haven't we received a response to our request up until now?

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.180
Oops!

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:22.240
Are you all right?

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:23.490
Who are you?

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:34.890
You totally groped her, didn't you?

00:11:34.890 --> 00:11:35.900
Huh?!

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:38.440
You lucked out, dog.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:41.160
I didn't... Hey! Come on!

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:44.340
Yolant!

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:59.280
Princess, you are a very courageous person who even piloted a mobile suit under the heat of battle.

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:04.140
You are also the successor of Lord Uzumi Nara Athha,

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:06.950
the great leader of Orb who refused to succumb to pressure

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:09.580
and stayed true to his belief in a utopia.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:16.290
So how should we act given the current state of the world?

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:19.460
I'm sure you know the answer to that very well.

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:23.010
We will protect and maintain the ideals of our nation.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:24.740
It's as simple as that.

00:12:25.620 --> 00:12:29.390
We will not invade anyone, nor will we allow anyone to invade us.

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:32.080
We will not intervene in the conflicts of other nations.

00:12:32.740 --> 00:12:33.620
That's right.

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:37.060
We believe the same as well.

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:39.900
That is of course the preferred course of action.

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:43.680
However, without power, that just isn't possible.

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:47.160
I'm sure, Princess, that you would also... no...

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:49.120
You would understand this fact even better than us.

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:54.710
And that's why Orb also maintains full military facilities, am I right?

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:59.250
Will you please stop calling me "Princess".

00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:03.540
Please excuse me, Representative Athha.

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:08.100
However, I have to wonder...

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:11.430
What are you so afraid of?

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:15.310
Pressure from the Atlantic Federation?

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:19.400
Perhaps they'd accuse Orb of providing us with military assistance, thereby breaking the treaty's agreements?{this line sucks}

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:24.820
But, of course, there's no evidence to back that up.

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:33.160
Although it is a fact that after the battle with Orb, we welcomed its refugees with open arms.

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:42.550
Who are you or I to judge these people who merely took advantage of their technical skills to make a living here.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:11.400
However, too much power will lead to another conflict!

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:19.340
What's going on?

00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:26.920
Auel, above you!

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:30.300
No, Princess.

00:14:30.940 --> 00:14:34.970
Power is necessary because there will always be conflict.

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:43.390
Sting!

00:14:43.390 --> 00:14:44.920
Okay! Let's go!

00:14:58.060 --> 00:14:58.840
How's it look?

00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:00.760
<i>Okay. The information was accurate.</i>

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:01.710
<i>All's good.</i>

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:04.710
Starting quantum catalysis. Power flow satisfactory.

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:07.880
All armor active. All weapons accessible.

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:10.510
System operating on "combat status."

00:15:47.140 --> 00:15:47.920
A warning siren?!

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:48.860
What happened?!

00:15:48.860 --> 00:15:49.720
Hangar six?!

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:50.840
What is it?

00:15:57.240 --> 00:15:57.700
Cagalli!

00:15:57.700 --> 00:15:58.140
Mr. Chairman!

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:09.100
Chaos?! Gaia?! Abyss?!

00:16:09.100 --> 00:16:12.450
Destroy the hangars first! 
They'll be coming with mobile suits!

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:14.410
Stella! You take the left!

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:15.240
Okay.

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:28.710
Send 'em out right away!

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:30.670
They're the new models from Hangar six!

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:32.090
Someone's taken them!

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:35.050
Send out our mobile suits! We've gotta stop them!

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:36.140
What did he say?!

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:37.800
New models?

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:45.330
Why that's...

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:46.400
A Gundam?!

00:17:08.280 --> 00:17:10.750
Take the Princess to the shelter! Where's Evans?!

00:17:11.820 --> 00:17:12.700
This way!

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:15.460
Cagalli!

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:19.970
We cannot let them through!

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:22.350
Contact the Minerva and ask for backup!

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:24.520
Arthur! Where is he?!

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:31.480
Athrun...

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:37.910
This way!

00:17:48.520 --> 00:17:49.790
Damn!

00:17:50.360 --> 00:17:53.050
Why? Why's this happening?!

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:03.140
Athrun.

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:04.020
I'm all right.

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:19.580
Come on!

00:18:21.360 --> 00:18:25.960
<i>Impulse, standby for takeoff. Pilot, proceed to Core Splendor.</i>

00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:30.760
<i>Sword Module selected. Opening Silhouette Hangar two.</i>

00:18:30.760 --> 00:18:33.730
<i>Silhouette Flyer, standby for takeoff.</i>

00:18:33.730 --> 00:18:38.190
<i>Platform setup complete. Central catapult, online.</i>

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:40.550
<i>Opening airtight shutters</i>.

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:44.100
<i>Emergency crew, standby for takeoff plan.</i>

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:47.320
<i>Raise central catapult to launch position!</i>

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:53.110
<i>Core Splendor, all systems online. Commencing takeoff sequence.</i>

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:58.040
<i>Hatch opened. Linear launch system engaged.</i>

00:18:58.600 --> 00:19:02.120
<i>Catapult power levels normal. Course clear.</i>

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:04.410
<i>Core Splendor, take off.</i>

00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:20.510
<i>Catapult engaged. Deploy Silhouette Flyer.</i>

00:19:26.460 --> 00:19:29.860
<i>Next, deploy Chest Flyer.</i>

00:19:33.580 --> 00:19:36.900
<i>Deploy Leg Flyer.</i>

00:19:39.660 --> 00:19:40.240
Get in!

00:19:40.600 --> 00:19:41.280
What?!

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:48.580
You...

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:51.680
I can't let you die in a place like this!

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:15.770
What now?

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:21.450
What?!

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:30.370
This guy...

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:51.600
Stella!

00:20:52.860 --> 00:20:53.730
Another one!

00:21:40.840 --> 00:21:41.400
What?!

00:22:03.840 --> 00:22:05.360
Why is this happening?

00:22:06.040 --> 00:22:08.760
Do you guys wanna start another war?!

00:22:11.810 --> 00:22:17.280
<i>No, Princess. Power is necessary because there will always be conflict.</i>

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:25.350
<b>kotoba wo kasanete mo wakari aenai koto</b>

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:25.350
I still did not realize

00:22:24.940 --> 00:22:32.160
<b>
mada shiranakatta ne</b>

00:22:24.940 --> 00:22:32.160
That there are things that can't be conveyed even with words

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:39.810
<b>kimi dake wo dakishimetakute nakushita yume kimi wa</b>

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:39.810
My lost dreams of wanting to hold you by my side,

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:46.770
<b>
"akiramenaide" to itta</b>

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:46.770
For them, you said, "Don't give up!"

00:22:46.340 --> 00:22:53.600
<b>tooku hanareteru hodo ni chikaku ni kanjiteru</b>

00:22:46.340 --> 00:22:53.600
The further we are apart, the nearer I feel you are

00:22:53.180 --> 00:23:01.740
<b>
samishisa mo tsuyosa eto kawatteku... kimi wo omottanara</b>

00:22:53.180 --> 00:23:01.740
Even my loneliness turns into strength... when I think of you

00:23:01.350 --> 00:23:08.430
